# YOUR OWN CHOICES, and nothing else.
#
# This file is searched before every system table, so a row here is a decision
# that outranks whatever the desktop ships — which is why KDOS ships none of
# its own defaults in it. `Open With` writes here when you tick "always".
#
# The defaults live at /etc/xdg: `kdos-mimeapps.list` for the compositor,
# `kdos-console-mimeapps.list` for the console, and `mimeapps.list` for what
# both desktops agree on. Anything you put here beats all three.

[Default Applications]
